shadow 4.20.0 no longer builds the expiry utility: it was dropped upstream, so
src/expiry.c is gone and src/Makefile.am installs only
"faillog chage chfn chsh gpasswd newgrp passwd" into ubindir.

The image initial-script still chmods it, so prepare-image.sh aborts with
"chmod: cannot access '/usr/bin/expiry': No such file or directory" whenever an
image element is built rather than pulled from a cache. Keep chage, which shadow
4.20.0 still installs, and drop only expiry.

Upstream-bug: https://gitlab.com/freedesktop-sdk/freedesktop-sdk/-/issues
---
--- a/elements/components/shadow.bst
+++ b/elements/components/shadow.bst
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
       for i in su passwd gpasswd chsh chfn newgrp; do
         chmod 4755 "${sysroot}%{bindir}/${i}"
       done
-      for i in expiry chage; do
+      for i in chage; do
         chmod 4755 "${sysroot}%{bindir}/${i}"
       done
       # If those fail, please use components/fakecap.bst in LD_PRELOAD
